    "interconnection": "A single slow tidal carrier takes a lantern through a duct too short for its knight. The knight leaves for the anvil and patrol gallery, then turns the vertical tide gate into a return balcony. That frees the same carrier. Intercept its cargo from above and use the far recoil dock to bring it back over the gallery. The last tally opens the beam lane above the original fire, so the returned lantern becomes necessary shade.",
    "solution": "Board the freight and leave its lantern aboard. Pogo the dock anvil to the upper gallery; time the low sweep, stationary knot and curved patrol from the broad pauses between them. Jump over the tide-gate hub and cut down, rotating it into a balcony and releasing the blocked freight. Drop onto its broad deck, recover the lantern, and cross to the far recoil dock. Compress with Down while carrying, release, and jump late with its rising lift to the upper tally. Return west over the same patrol gallery carrying shade, then glide down into the opened low beam corridor above your original fire.",
    "novelty": "The freight and player take different heights around one continuous obstacle. The outward blade route opens the returning cargo route. The final tally opens the starting exit passage, whose overhead beams require the same lantern brought back across the gallery. The cargo is a real moving source of shade rather than a consumed key.",
    "nearestExisting": "F55/F56 continuous moving hazards, F18 returning cargo and B35 load/release transport are combined around one tide gate and one lantern.",
